  "definition": "Calculation of Basic Reserves",
  "effectiveDate": "2017-07-25",
  "historyNote": "#7419, eff 7-1-01; ss by #9516, eff 7-25-09; ss by #12219, eff 7-25-17",
  "inScheme": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/scheme",
  "notation": "Ins 3505.01",
  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ins3500.html",
  "prefLabel": "Ins 3505.01 Calculation of Basic Reserves",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ins 3505.01 Calculation of Basic Reserves.\n\n(a) Basic reserves shall be calculated as the greater of the segmented reserves and the unitary reserves. Both the segmented reserves and the unitary reserves for any policy shall use the same valuation mortality table and selection factors. At the option of the insurer, in calculating segmented reserves and net premiums, either of the adjustments described in paragraph (1) or (2) below may be made:\n\n(1) Treat the unitary reserve, if greater than zero, applicable at the end of each segment as a pure endowment and subtract the unitary reserve, if greater than zero, applicable at the beginning of each segment from the present value of guaranteed life insurance and endowment benefits for each segment; or\n\n(2) Treat the guaranteed cash surrender value, if greater than zero, applicable at the end of each segment as a pure endowment and subtract the guaranteed cash surrender value, if greater than zero, applicable at the beginning of each segment from the present value of guaranteed life insurance and endowment benefits for each segment.\n\nSource. #7419, eff 7-1-01; ss by #9516, eff 7-25-09; ss by #12219, eff 7-25-17",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ins3500.html"
}
